GameEngine overlay patch for yoga 3.2.1.

algorithm: key a measured node's cache entries by owner size when its measured
size depends on the owner.

calculateLayoutInternal reuses a measure-function node's cached size through
canUseCachedMeasurement, which compares available sizes and sizing modes only.
Two of its rules accept an entry measured under a different available size:
newSizeIsStricterAndStillValid (a tighter fit-content constraint the old size
still fits) and oldSizeIsMaxContentAndStillFits. Both assume the measured size is
a function of the available size alone. It is not when the node's min/max size,
padding or margin is a percentage: measureNodeWithMeasureFunc resolves those
against ownerWidth/ownerHeight, which no cache entry records.

The failing case: a label with flex: 0 1 auto and min-width: 37% in a 700 px
row measures 259 (37% of 700) while computing its flex basis. The row narrows
to 400 px; the label's available width goes 700 -> 400 fit-content, 259 still
fits, so the stricter rule returns 259 where a fresh layout gives 148
(37% of 400), as CSS does: a percentage min-width resolves against the
containing block of the current layout. A min-height percentage fails the
same way when the owner gets shorter. A percentage max-width or max-height does
not leave a stale size: constrainMaxSizeForMode narrows the available size
handed to the measurement, and the flex line re-applies the max clamp. Only a
percentage floor lets the larger, stale size survive.

The fix records the owner size on every measure-function cache entry and, for a
node whose style carries a percentage min/max dimension, padding or margin,
accepts an entry only under the same owner size. Nodes without such a
percentage keep every relaxed rule, so text in a resizing panel without
percentage constraints is measured exactly as often as before. Nodes without a
measure function are not touched: their cache only accepts an exact match of
available size and mode.

The gate also covers percentage max sizes, padding and margins, which resolve
against the owner during measurement too, and it compares both owner axes for
any of them. A node with only a percentage min-width is therefore re-measured
when only its owner's height changes; keying per axis would avoid that extra
measurement at the cost of a wider gate. CachedMeasurement grows by two floats
(72 bytes per node over the nine entries); nothing allocates.

Upstream main (facebook/yoga, Cache.cpp and calculateLayoutInternal, read
2026-10-12) has the same rules and no owner-size key.

diff --git a/yoga/algorithm/CalculateLayout.cpp b/yoga/algorithm/CalculateLayout.cpp
index 0065096..2eb72ee 100644
--- a/yoga/algorithm/CalculateLayout.cpp
+++ b/yoga/algorithm/CalculateLayout.cpp
@@ -2150,6 +2150,38 @@ static void calculateLayoutImpl(
   }
 }
 
+// A measured node's percentage min/max sizes, padding and margins resolve
+// against its owner's size, but canUseCachedMeasurement only compares available
+// sizes. Its relaxed rules (a stricter fit-content constraint the old size still
+// fits, a max-content size that still fits) then hand back a size clamped or
+// padded against the previous owner: a short label with min-width: 37% keeps
+// 37% of the wide row after the row narrows. Such a node's cache entries are
+// valid only under the owner size they were measured with.
+static bool measuredSizeDependsOnOwnerSize(const yoga::Node* const node) {
+  const auto& style = node->style();
+  for (const Dimension dimension : {Dimension::Width, Dimension::Height}) {
+    if (style.minDimension(dimension).unit() == Unit::Percent ||
+        style.maxDimension(dimension).unit() == Unit::Percent) {
+      return true;
+    }
+  }
+  for (const Edge edge : ordinals<Edge>()) {
+    if (style.padding(edge).unit() == Unit::Percent ||
+        style.margin(edge).unit() == Unit::Percent) {
+      return true;
+    }
+  }
+  return false;
+}
+
+static bool cachedOwnerSizeMatches(
+    const CachedMeasurement& entry,
+    const float ownerWidth,
+    const float ownerHeight) {
+  return yoga::inexactEquals(entry.ownerWidth, ownerWidth) &&
+      yoga::inexactEquals(entry.ownerHeight, ownerHeight);
+}
+
 //
 // This is a wrapper around the calculateLayoutImpl function. It determines
 // whether the layout request is redundant and can be skipped.
@@ -2203,6 +2235,7 @@ bool calculateLayoutInternal(
   // they are the most expensive to measure, so it's worth avoiding redundant
   // measurements if at all possible.
   if (node->hasMeasureFunc()) {
+    const bool ownerSizeKeyed = measuredSizeDependsOnOwnerSize(node);
     const float marginAxisRow =
         node->style().computeMarginForAxis(FlexDirection::Row, ownerWidth);
     const float marginAxisColumn =
@@ -2222,7 +2255,10 @@ bool calculateLayoutInternal(
             layout->cachedLayout.computedHeight,
             marginAxisRow,
             marginAxisColumn,
-            node->getConfig())) {
+            node->getConfig()) &&
+        (!ownerSizeKeyed ||
+         cachedOwnerSizeMatches(
+             layout->cachedLayout, ownerWidth, ownerHeight))) {
       cachedResults = &layout->cachedLayout;
     } else {
       // Try to use the measurement cache.
@@ -2240,7 +2276,10 @@ bool calculateLayoutInternal(
                 layout->cachedMeasurements[i].computedHeight,
                 marginAxisRow,
                 marginAxisColumn,
-                node->getConfig())) {
+                node->getConfig()) &&
+            (!ownerSizeKeyed ||
+             cachedOwnerSizeMatches(
+                 layout->cachedMeasurements[i], ownerWidth, ownerHeight))) {
           cachedResults = &layout->cachedMeasurements[i];
           break;
         }
@@ -2325,6 +2364,8 @@ bool calculateLayoutInternal(
           layout->measuredDimension(Dimension::Width);
       newCacheEntry->computedHeight =
           layout->measuredDimension(Dimension::Height);
+      newCacheEntry->ownerWidth = ownerWidth;
+      newCacheEntry->ownerHeight = ownerHeight;
     }
   }
 
diff --git a/yoga/node/CachedMeasurement.h b/yoga/node/CachedMeasurement.h
index 9c76280..e150fef 100644
--- a/yoga/node/CachedMeasurement.h
+++ b/yoga/node/CachedMeasurement.h
@@ -25,6 +25,12 @@ struct CachedMeasurement {
   float computedWidth{-1};
   float computedHeight{-1};
 
+  // The owner size the entry was measured under. Only consulted for a node
+  // whose measured size depends on it (a percentage min/max size, padding or
+  // margin), see measuredSizeDependsOnOwnerSize in CalculateLayout.cpp.
+  float ownerWidth{-1};
+  float ownerHeight{-1};
+
   bool operator==(CachedMeasurement measurement) const {
     bool isEqual = widthSizingMode == measurement.widthSizingMode &&
         heightSizingMode == measurement.heightSizingMode;
@@ -46,6 +52,15 @@ struct CachedMeasurement {
       isEqual = isEqual && computedHeight == measurement.computedHeight;
     }
 
+    if (!yoga::isUndefined(ownerWidth) ||
+        !yoga::isUndefined(measurement.ownerWidth)) {
+      isEqual = isEqual && ownerWidth == measurement.ownerWidth;
+    }
+    if (!yoga::isUndefined(ownerHeight) ||
+        !yoga::isUndefined(measurement.ownerHeight)) {
+      isEqual = isEqual && ownerHeight == measurement.ownerHeight;
+    }
+
     return isEqual;
   }
 };
